		c	Given an ellipse defined by the equation {@code (x/a)^2 + (y/b)^2 = 1}, where {@code a} and {@code b} are the semi-major and semi-minor axes respectively, this computes the distance between an arbitrary point and the ellipse.\nThe point (x, y) is within the ellipse if the return value is < 0, outside the ellipse if the return value is > 0 and exactly on the edge of the ellipse if the return value is 0.
